@@ -506,0 +507,3 @@
+- **Prompts to an external driver are checked for the local account name before launch (experiment; card 376 retro, Decider D240).** While this entry is on trial: before any prompt is sent to an external model service (the vote runner, `cursor_reply.py`, `cursor_write.py`, `muse_write.py`, `llm_check_when_back.py` and any direct `grok`, `agy` or `codex` call), the launcher runs `home_paths.find_accounts` with `home_paths.local_accounts()` over the prompt bytes (the account name only, form F10; the path forms F1 to F9 are not part of this check, so a prompt that quotes a planted sample is not refused) and refuses to launch (exit non-zero, naming `line:form`, never the matched text) on any hit; a prompt built from a diff, a log or a record is passed through `home_paths.scrub_account_bytes` first, because a diff of a card that removes a name carries the removed lines; each launch appends one line (launcher, sha256 of the prompt as sent, number of hits, result) to `.mob/records/<card>/prompt-checks.jsonl`, so the check's execution is a committed artifact and the gate reviewer checks that every external seat of the card has a line; a refused launch is also one line in the card's retro input; the check and its planted-fail tests are written red first as a tooling card filed with this pick, and until it lands the facilitator counts the name in each prompt by hand (`grep -c -w -e "$USERNAME"` on the prompt file, which prints a number only) and scrubs before sending.
+  - Hypothesis: a launcher that refuses a prompt holding the account name stops the name reaching an outside service. Metric: prompts sent to an external service that held the account name (card 376: 1, the second-review prompt, caught by a hand count after it was sent), target 0. Counter-metric: launches refused by a false positive, and seconds added per launch. Trial: the next 3 cards, counted from Decider D240. Owner: the facilitator.
